# Indian Banking Sector – Stock Market Analysis

## Project Overview

This project analyzes five major Indian banking stocks using Python and financial analytics techniques.

The stocks analyzed are:

- HDFC Bank
- ICICI Bank
- Kotak Mahindra Bank
- Axis Bank
- State Bank of India (SBI)

The analysis uses two years of daily adjusted closing-price data from 14 August 2024 to 14 August 2026.

## Objectives

The project evaluates the selected banking stocks using:

- Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
- Stock price and return analysis
- Risk and volatility analysis
- Sharpe ratio
- Maximum drawdown
- Moving averages
- Rolling volatility
- Linear Regression
- Logistic Regression
- K-Means Clustering
- Data visualization

## Tools and Libraries

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- yfinance

## Key Findings

- SBI recorded the highest cumulative return of 38.08% and an annualised return of 18.77% during the study period.
- Kotak Mahindra Bank recorded the lowest annualised volatility at 18.67% and the shallowest maximum drawdown at -18.37%.
- The Logistic Regression model achieved 56.38% classification accuracy for HDFC Bank, indicating limited short-term predictability using the selected historical price-based features.
- K-Means clustering grouped the five banking stocks according to their risk-return characteristics.

## Data Source

Historical daily adjusted closing-price data was obtained from Yahoo Finance using the `yfinance` Python library.

